.TH SEEDCHECK 1 "October 2026" "seedcheck 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
seedcheck \- test cloud-init configurations across Ubuntu releases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B seedcheck run
.I CONFIG
.RB [ \-\-release
.IR REL ]...
.RB [ \-\-markdown
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-json
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-artifacts\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR SECONDS ]
.RB [ \-\-keep ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.br
.B seedcheck validate
.I CONFIG
.br
.B seedcheck releases
.br
.B seedcheck \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B seedcheck
answers one question: does this cloud-init configuration work on every
Ubuntu release I care about?
Given a
.I seedcheck.yaml
file that points to a cloud-init user-data file and lists expectations, it
validates the user-data, launches one LXD container per Ubuntu release with
it, waits for cloud-init to finish, runs checks inside each container
(installed packages, service states, files, users, custom commands and
cloud-init's own error report), prints a pass/fail matrix with checks as
rows and releases as columns, and always deletes its containers.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI run " CONFIG"
Validate, launch, check and report.
.TP
.BI validate " CONFIG"
Statically validate the configuration and its user-data, without launching
anything. Does not need LXD.
.TP
.B releases
List the supported releases, their codenames and LXD images.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-release " REL"
Only test this release, given as a version (22.04) or a codename (jammy).
Repeatable. Overrides the configuration.
.TP
.BI \-\-markdown " PATH"
Also write the matrix as Markdown, suitable for a GitHub job summary.
.TP
.BI \-\-json " PATH"
Also write the full results as JSON.
.TP
.BI \-\-artifacts\-dir " DIR"
Save each container's cloud-init logs under
.IR DIR / RELEASE /.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
How long to wait for each release; overrides the configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-keep
Do not delete the containers, for debugging.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show every lxc command and its output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every check on every release passed or only warned.
.TP
.B 1
At least one check failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage, configuration or user-data, found before any container started.
.TP
.B 3
Infrastructure error: LXD is unusable, or a release ended in error.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted; the containers are still deleted.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to a non-empty value, the matrix is printed without color.
Color is also disabled when standard output is not a terminal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
seedcheck validate examples/nginx/seedcheck.yaml
seedcheck run examples/nginx/seedcheck.yaml \-\-markdown report.md
seedcheck run seedcheck.yaml \-\-release noble \-\-keep \-v
.fi
.SH NOTES
LXD is distributed as a snap, so it cannot be a package dependency.
Install and initialize it with
.BR "sudo snap install lxd && sudo lxd init \-\-auto" ,
then add yourself to the
.B lxd
group.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lxc (1),
.BR cloud-init (1)
.PP
https://github.com/oum255/seedcheck
